= Tariffs and Cuts

Broad tariffs rattle markets. Aid and research grants are frozen. Thousands of federal employees are dismissed. The administration claims a mandate. The courts, Congress, and the public all push back, unevenly.

- @economy: Make the economic case.
- @rights: Make the rule-of-law case.
- @mobilize: Mobilize protests.

@economy
subtitle: Kitchen-table politics.
on-arrival: pop_mod += 0.4; mod_dissent -= 2; stability += 1

Prices, jobs, and retirement accounts become the focus. The message resonates.

@rights
subtitle: Principled.
on-arrival: stability += 3; media_trust += 2; enthusiasm += 2

We argue that the government is not following the law. Many voters agree and many do not care.

@mobilize
subtitle: Mass energy.
on-arrival: enthusiasm += 5; far_left += 1; pop_mod += 0.2

Protests grow and stay peaceful, overwhelmingly.
